The last patches for nethack (a GREAT game!), p05
screw up the graphics characters on unix systems. If the meta
character is used from the NETHACKOPTIONS=graphics: \mq etc.
the character that is actually printed is not the one that is wanted.

The problem can be solved (very quick & dirty) by commenting out
the second define of g_putch in pri.c. The ifdefs there think
we are using the ibm charset :-(.

I hope this helps other unix players, and that it is fixed in a
more solid way in patch p06.

Keep up the good work guys.

